  "title": "SIKH EMPIRE: AR gobindshahi rupee (10.49g), Amritsar, VS1865. EF",
  "description": "SIKH EMPIRE: AR gobindshahi rupee (10.49g), Amritsar, VS1865, KM-A20.2, Herrli-01.20.04, slight weakness of strike, EF, S, ex Jess A. Yockers Collection.    From our own examination, it appears that the gobindshahi rupee followed a standard of about 10.95-11.00g from VS1841-1852, then about 10.75g from VS1854-1860, and finally about 10.65g from VS1862-1865, then restored to the nanakshahi rupee standard of about 11.15g when reestablished in VS1895 until the last gobindshahi rupee in VS1905.",
